From 82fa15fe12d6f0cf75a12fa7eca6868d19864747 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:26:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] slot 7: chip-core Verilog uses the 13 custom-pad core
 nets

verilog/rtl/chipalooza_frame.v: ports s7_an[1:0], s7_an_0_esd and
s7_an_1_esd replaced by the 13 nets s7_an_0_* / s7_an_1_*, connected by
name to slot7_wrapper.  verilog/gl/sg13cmos5l_ocd_chipalooza.v: the same
13 nets between padframe and harness_core; the pads s7_an[1:0] remain chip
pins only.  verilog/rtl/digital_tb.v: the 13 ports left open.
validate/lvs/blackboxes.v regenerated (gen_blackboxes.py).

Checked: iverilog elaborates chipalooza_frame with dut.v (cocotb setup)
before and after, identical warnings.  Not changed: xschem schematics and
symbols, validate/lvs/chipalooza_frame.struct.v (needs yosys).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XU3KH5LbmFCchnNvtB8nAZ
